  "label": "User projected onto the patient in the rectal exam scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the patient in the lower panel of the meme, who is depicted as embarrassed and uncomfortable during a rectal exam. This projection is implied by the meme's structure: the top text addresses 'Mark' (Zuckerberg) as if he is the one being embarrassed, and the bottom text describes a common, awkward male reaction during a medical procedure. The user, by viewing the meme, is implicitly identifying with the patient's experience of embarrassment and discomfort, even though the patient is not explicitly labeled 'you'. The humor and the framing suggest the user is meant to imagine themselves in the patient's shoes, experiencing the same awkwardness. The projection is onto the 'embarrassed_patient_exam' scene, which is the core visual and textual context for the user's identification.",
